# Test project (`RagDataTools.UnitTests`)

## Scope

- Use unit tests for chunking strategies, regex providers, connector helpers, ingest helpers, and other leaf components.
- Keep end-to-end behavior in production code and test-data builders separate from strategy classes.
- Prefer fluent builders/helpers for chunking fixtures when a scenario needs code blocks, tables, images, info blocks, strange-word text, topic hierarchies, or code block count ranges.

## Test style

- Use `NUnit`, `FluentAssertions`, `Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk`, `AutoFixture`, and `Moq.AutoMock`.
- Every test method must use `// Arrange`, `// Act`, `// Assert` in that order.
- Do not use imperative loops in test bodies.
- Test names must follow `<methodname>_When<conditionbeingchecked>_Should<expectedresult>`.

## Test data

- Keep reusable chunking fixtures under `RagDataTools.UnitTests/TestData` and `RagDataTools.UnitTests/Chunkers/TestData`.
- Prefer canonical fixture shapes for `ChunkModel`, `RelationshipType`, and related test data types.
